Default hostname is fishball, not Fishball7020

A shorter name, and one that does not need shift-key gymnastics every time you
type ssh root@... or an mDNS URI. The board answers to fishball.local.

This is a new patch rather than an edit to 0013 because 0013 has been applied to
trees already: setup.sh cannot re-apply a patch over its own earlier version, so
changing one in place breaks every checkout that has it.

The name is still per-board: fw_setenv hostname <name> overrides the built-in
default without a rebuild, and ./devkit net name <name> does that and finds the
board again afterwards. Setting it back to pluto restores compatibility with
tooling that expects pluto.local.
diff --git a/buildroot/configs/zynq_pluto_defconfig b/buildroot/configs/zynq_pluto_defconfig
--- a/buildroot/configs/zynq_pluto_defconfig
+++ b/buildroot/configs/zynq_pluto_defconfig
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL=y
 BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_LINARO_ARM=y
 BR2_OPTIMIZE_2=y
-BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_HOSTNAME="Fishball7020"
+BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_HOSTNAME="fishball"
 BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ISSUE="Welcome to Pluto"
 BR2_ROOTFS_DEVICE_CREATION_DYNAMIC_MDEV=y
 BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ROOT_PASSWD="analog"
